Subject: The generator can read each function's closure-variable table

What this does
  - `JSAotGenFunc` gains `closure_count`, `closure_type[]` and `closure_idx[]`, copied from the function bytecode's `closure_var` table in `js_aot_gen_collect` and released in `js_aot_gen_free`. Entry i describes the variable behind `get_var_ref` / `put_var_ref` i: the engine's closure type (local or argument of the creating function, or one of its own closure variables) and its index.

Why we need it
  The offline analysis models every closure variable of a program as one shared node, so one unknown write (the Octane harness's `continuation = continuation()`) poisons every captured variable, leaves calls through captured objects unresolved, and keeps whole call trees from being analysed. To give each variable its own cell the generator has to follow a `get_var_ref` index to the function that declares the variable.

Soundness
  Generator-side data only: nothing on the run-time paths changes, the table is read once when the generator collects the program's functions.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -69539,0 +69540,17 @@
+                if (b->closure_var_count > 0 && b->closure_var != NULL) {
+                    uint8_t *cty = js_malloc_rt(rt, (size_t)b->closure_var_count);
+                    uint16_t *cix = js_malloc_rt(rt, sizeof(uint16_t) * (size_t)b->closure_var_count);
+                    if (cty && cix) {
+                        int ci;
+                        for (ci = 0; ci < b->closure_var_count; ci++) {
+                            cty[ci] = b->closure_var[ci].closure_type;
+                            cix[ci] = b->closure_var[ci].var_idx;
+                        }
+                        g->closure_count = b->closure_var_count;
+                        g->closure_type = cty;
+                        g->closure_idx = cix;
+                    } else {
+                        js_free_rt(rt, cty);
+                        js_free_rt(rt, cix);
+                    }
+                }
@@ -69580,0 +69598,2 @@
+            js_free_rt(rt, (void *)arr[i].closure_type);
+            js_free_rt(rt, (void *)arr[i].closure_idx);
--- a/quickjs-aot-gen.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-gen.h
@@ -76,0 +77,6 @@
+    /* The closure-variable table: entry i is the variable behind get_var_ref / put_var_ref i. `closure_type[i]` is the engine's closure type (0 = a local of the
+       creating function, 1 = an argument of it, 2 = a closure variable of it, others = global / module forms) and `closure_idx[i]` the variable's index in that
+       function (locals and arguments are indexed apart). The generator follows a variable to its declaring function with these and the creators' `cpool_fn`. */
+    int closure_count;
+    const uint8_t *closure_type;
